lesson k-push-pull-float-sink v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=1 subject=physics levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Push and pull, float and sink"
  goal "Say whether a force is a push or a pull, which push is bigger, and whether a thing floats or sinks."

  look {
    scene 30x14 {
      row all at=canvas(1, 1) space=3 align=end {
        forces f thing=box push=5 labels=false
        tank t float=2 sunk=1 letters=false
      }
    }
    say """
      A push moves a thing away from you and a pull brings it towards you. A longer arrow is a bigger
      push. In the tank some things float at the top of the water and some sink to the bottom.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.push-or-pull-arrow p=1 thing="box" level=medium
    }
    practice k.push-or-pull-arrow count=2 seed=2 easy-count=1
    practice k.push-or-pull-job count=2 seed=3
    practice k.bigger-push count=1 seed=4
    show k.float-or-sink k=1
    practice k.how-many-float count=2 seed=5
    show k.float-or-sink k=0
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.tug a=7 b=4 easy-a=8 easy-b=3 hard-a=6 hard-b=4
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.more-floaters f=2 easy-f=1 hard-f=3
  }
  remember {
    say "A push goes away, a pull comes towards you. Things float at the top or sink to the bottom."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question aloud. Pushes and pulls are best felt: push a chair, pull a drawer, and say
    which it is. For floating, a washing-up bowl and some things from the kitchen do more than any
    page. If the child is stuck on the arrows, point to where the hand would be. Off the page, guess
    whether each thing will float before you drop it in the bath. Japan, 幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten
    guidelines), 環境, 内容 (2): "生活の中で，様々な物に触れ，その性質や仕組みに興味や関心をもつ。"
    (Touch many things in daily life and take an interest in how they behave and work.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level a push on the box is named in the teacher's pen first, the pushes to compare are very different, and one or two things float."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the arrows are on a trolley and a ball, the pushes to compare are close, and three or four things float before the corks go in."
  }
}
